.\" offload(1) manpage — mdoc format
.Dd May 28, 2026
.Dt OFFLOAD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm offload
.Nd poka-yoke disk offload tool for macOS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -target-home Ar path
.Ar subcommand
.Op Ar args ...
.Op Fl -apply
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
moves heavy, low-velocity user data out of
.Pa $HOME
onto an external drive, replacing each source path with a symlink.
A guard launcher refuses to start an app whose data lives on an unmounted
volume.
The tool is mistake-proof by design: dry-run is the default, signature
verification precedes every destructive step, and all operations are
idempotent.
.Pp
The
.Cm protected
subcommand operates on TCC/FDA-protected paths
.Pq Path Pa Library/Messages , Path Pa Library/Application Support/MobileSync
and must be invoked from a
.Em separate
macOS Admin account whose Terminal has been granted Full Disk Access.
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width 18n
.It Cm help
Print the embedded long-form documentation
.Pq the script header is the single source of truth .
.It Cm version
Print the script version.
.It Cm status
Disk space, recent log entries, and any pending admin todo.
.It Cm list
.Va OFFLOAD_APPS
entries and the current state of each
.Pq Pa on-disk , symlinked , absent .
.It Cm checklist
Generate a progress checklist that reflects current state.
.It Cm launch Ar BundleName
Guarded launch. Refuses with a macOS dialog if the app's symlinked
data directory points to an unmounted volume.
.It Cm move Ar target Op Fl -apply
Execute a move tier.
Default is dry-run; supply
.Fl -apply
to actually mutate.
.It Cm protected Ar subcmd Op Fl -apply
Admin-mode subcommand. Requires
.Fl -target-home
pointing at a different user's home, an admin-group caller, and
Terminal-granted FDA.
.El
.Sh MOVE TARGETS
.Bl -tag -width 22n
.It Cm tier-c-cruft
Sweep
.Va node_modules , .venv , venv , target , build , dist , __pycache__ , .next
under
.Pa <TARGET_HOME>/Documents/Projects/GitHub .
.It Cm tier-b-downloads
Sort
.Pa <TARGET_HOME>/Downloads :
ROM zips matching common Nintendo/Sega names go to
.Pa $OFFLOAD_HOT/ROMs ;
everything else is archived to
.Pa $OFFLOAD_COLD/Archive/Downloads-<user>-<date>/ .
.It Cm tier-b-clones
.Xr rsync 1
with
.Fl -update
.Pq newer-mtime-wins
from
.Pa <TARGET_HOME>/Documents/Projects/Clones
into
.Pa $OFFLOAD_HOT/Clones .
.It Cm tier-a-app Ar Label
Relocate a single entry from
.Va OFFLOAD_APPS .
.It Cm tier-a-all
Iterate every entry in
.Va OFFLOAD_APPS .
.It Cm tier-a-simulator
Relocate
.Pa <TARGET_HOME>/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator .
.El
.Sh PROTECTED SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width 14n
.It Cm list
Inventory the protected paths under
.Fl -target-home .
.It Cm messages
Relocate
.Pa <TARGET_HOME>/Library/Messages .
.It Cm ios-backups
Relocate
.Pa <TARGET_HOME>/Library/Application Support/MobileSync/Backup .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width 22n
.It Fl -target-home Ar path
Operate on a different user's home. Triggers admin-mode invariants:
caller must NOT be the target user, must be in the
.Cm admin
group, and (for
.Cm protected
subcommands) Terminal must have Full Disk Access.
Defaults to
.Pa $HOME .
.It Fl -apply
Actually mutate. Without it, every operation is a dry-run that
prints intent only.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Drive paths come from environment variables
.Ev OFFLOAD_HOT
and
.Ev OFFLOAD_COLD ,
or from a config file at
.Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/offload/offload.conf .
The config file is a sourced shell snippet:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
OFFLOAD_HOT=/Volumes/MyFastSSD
OFFLOAD_COLD=/Volumes/MyArchiveHDD
# optional: replace the default OFFLOAD_APPS list
OFFLOAD_APPS=(
  "Signal|<TARGET_HOME>/Library/Application Support/Signal|Signal"
)
.Ed
.Pp
In
.Va OFFLOAD_APPS
rows, the literal token
.Sy <TARGET_HOME>
is substituted at runtime with the effective target home.
.Sh DESIGN
.Nm
follows poka-yoke discipline: bad outcomes are structurally
prevented, not merely documented.
.Bl -enum
.It
.Sy Single source of truth.
.Va OFFLOAD_APPS
is read by every subcommand
.Pq Cm list , Cm checklist , Cm launch , Cm move ;
no duplicated copies anywhere.
.It
.Sy Dry-run by default.
Mutation requires
.Fl -apply .
There is no destructive default.
.It
.Sy Verify before delete.
Cross-volume moves
.Xr rsync 1
to destination, compare file count and total bytes against source,
and remove the source only on signature match.
.It
.Sy Idempotent.
Re-running a tier on a source that is already a valid symlink skips
cleanly. An existing destination is never silently overwritten.
.It
.Sy Never sudo from inside.
.Pq EACCES
failures append to
.Pa ~/offload-admin-todo.txt
and execution continues. At end-of-run a reviewable wrapper is
emitted at
.Pa ~/bin/offload-admin-pass
for the user to read and sudo themselves.
.It
.Sy Two-account workflow.
Standard data is moved by the owner.
.Pq TCC/FDA-protected
paths require a separate Admin account whose Terminal has Full Disk Access.
The
.Cm protected
subcommand enforces all three invariants before any work.
.It
.Sy Guard launcher.
After relocation, symlinked data becomes unreachable when the drive
is unmounted.
.Cm offload launch
checks the target before opening the app.
.It
.Sy Discovered exclusions.
macOS sandboxed containers
.Pq Pa ~/Library/Containers/com.apple.*
refuse to follow symlinks; excluded. Mail's storage is fragile under
symlinks; use Mail's Accounts preferences instead. Browser profiles
do constant SQLite writes; corruption is common; excluded from
defaults.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss First-time setup
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mkdir -p ~/.config/offload
cat > ~/.config/offload/offload.conf <<EOF
OFFLOAD_HOT=/Volumes/MyFastSSD
OFFLOAD_COLD=/Volumes/MyArchiveHDD
EOF
.Ed
.Ss Inspect
.Bd -literal -offset indent
offload status
offload list
offload checklist
.Ed
.Ss Safe first sweep
.Bd -literal -offset indent
offload move tier-c-cruft
offload move tier-c-cruft --apply
.Ed
.Ss Guarded launch
.Bd -literal -offset indent
offload launch Signal
.Ed
.Ss Admin running on another user's home
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# logged in as Admin account, Terminal has FDA
offload protected --target-home /Users/alice list
offload protected --target-home /Users/alice messages --apply
offload --target-home /Users/alice move tier-a-app Signal --apply
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width 36n
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/offload/offload.conf
User configuration: drive paths and optional
.Va OFFLOAD_APPS
override.
.It Pa ~/offload-YYYY-MM-DD.log
Per-run log, append-only.
.It Pa ~/offload-admin-todo.txt
Paths collected at run time when an operation failed with EACCES.
.It Pa ~/bin/offload-admin-pass
Emitted sudo-review script (only created when admin todo is non-empty).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Invariant violation, invalid input, or fatal error.
.It 2
Destination conflict; manual review required.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rsync 1 ,
.Xr tmutil 8 ,
.Xr ln 1 ,
.Xr launchctl 1
.Sh AUTHORS
Maintained in the Sage-is/homebrew-apps tap.
Bug reports:
.Lk https://github.com/Sage-is/homebrew-apps/issues
.Sh BUGS
The script never invokes
.Cm sudo
itself. Some user-space paths require elevated privileges to move;
those are captured in
.Pa ~/offload-admin-todo.txt
and emitted as a separate sudo-review script for manual execution.
This is intentional.
